WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.350
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
for my Game of Thrones video I wanted to talk

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:09.610
about the Sand Snakes. If you saw my video
last week I explained how the show is changing

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:13.610
things but for this video I’m going to talk
about all of them. They’re the 8 bastard

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:18.119
daughters of Oberyn Martell and various women.
The show has 3 of them, but the show cuts

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:19.220
characters out all the time so no surprise
there. When I get to the 5 that were cut out

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.680
I’ll also talk about why I think they chose
not to use them and what it means for the

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:25.869
story in season 5 versus the books.

00:00:25.869 --> 00:00:32.869
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do game of thrones videos every week.I even

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.700
do a weekly book giveaway all you have to
do to enter is be a subscriber and leave a

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.600
comment. I’ll explain more about that at
the end of all this.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.719
So if you’ve never heard of the Sand Snakes,
they’re Oberyn’s daughters. Oldest to

00:00:45.719 --> 00:00:52.719
youngest they are Obara, Nymeria, Tyene, Sarella,
Elia, Obella, Dorea and Loreza. The youngest

00:00:53.289 --> 00:00:58.100
four all belong to Ellaria. The woman you
saw with Oberyn in season 4 played by Indira

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:03.399
Varma. There’s no promise we’ll meet all
the mothers.

00:01:03.399 --> 00:01:08.320
The show is only focusing on Obara, Nymeria
and Tyene, the oldest ones. So because most

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.770
of you probably haven’t read the books I’m
going to talk about all of them oldest to

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:15.600
youngest and I’ll just save spoilery stuff
for the end and I’ll also talk about some

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:20.310
cool theories about Winds of Winter. George
RR Martin explained at comic con that all

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:23.630
of the Sand Snakes have really big roles in
that book.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:29.020
First is Obara Sand, on the show she’s being
played by Keisha Castle-Hughes. If you look

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.860
at the fan art version of her from the card
game she looks very different. I know this

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.850
will bug some of the book readers but the
show does this all the time. For instance

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:41.340
Yezzan in the book is supposed to look like
jabba the hutt and on the show this is what

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.380
the actor playing him looks like.

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.520
Just another day in television. Keisha is
a great actress that’s why they cast her.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.350
I think she’ll do the same type of special
fight training that they gave to Pedro Pascal.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.630
There’s some cool video of him learning
to use his weapon. Obara in the books always

00:01:55.630 --> 00:02:02.630
reminded me of a colder version of Brienne.
More militaristic and cunning.

00:02:02.719 --> 00:02:08.450
Regardless of what the show does, in the books
her mother was a whore from Oldtown. Her name

00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:12.569
is never mentioned but when Obara was old
enough Oberyn came to claim her. He threw

00:02:12.569 --> 00:02:16.640
a spear down at her feet and asked Obara to
choose between it and her mother. She chose

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:20.910
the spear. So that gives you an idea for what
kind of a life she prefers. As an adult her

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:24.540
weapons of choice are the signature spear
that you saw Oberyn use in his fight with

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.060
the Mountain, a whip and a round shield.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:32.250
When we first meet her in book 4 she’s about
30 years old and is described as being big-boned.

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:37.050
Meaning she looks like Brienne, she’s a
warrior. Which is why I was a little surprised

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:40.930
when they cast Keisha Castle-Hughes. But she
probably just blew them away in the casting

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:43.010
session so I’m optimistic.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.840
All of the Sand Snakes have varying degrees
of tempers, some are a little wilder than

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:51.640
others. Obara lives a very martial life, so
she respects the authority of her uncle Prince

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.050
Doran unlike her half sister Arianne.

00:02:54.050 --> 00:03:00.440
I’ll wait till we get to spoilers to talk
about what the show might be changing about

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:00.620
her.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:06.879
Next is Nymeria. On the show she’s being
played by Jessica Henwick. She’s about five

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:11.390
years younger than Obara and her mother was
a highborn woman from Volantis. That’s one

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:15.780
of the Free cities in the eastern continent.
It’s south of Braavos but still really far

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:18.670
away from slaver’s bay where Daenerys is
on the show.

00:03:18.670 --> 00:03:23.080
In the books she’s described much more like
you’d expect a highborn person to be, very

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:28.280
pale skin, high cheekbones, very slender.
Imagine a more willful future version of Sansa.

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:32.099
Which is kind of funny, because Sansa just
dyed her hair black like Nymeria at the end

00:03:32.099 --> 00:03:34.269
of season 4. Maybe she’ll take up poisons
too?

00:03:34.269 --> 00:03:39.080
To explain, Nymeria’s weapon of choice is
the dagger, she carries several on her. Because

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:44.120
it’s HBO and Dan and Dave got pretty salacious
with Oberyn’s Bi-Sexuality they’ll probably

00:03:44.120 --> 00:03:48.420
show Nymeria as bi-sexual too. It’s implied
that she’s a lesbian in feast for crows

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.700
but I don’t think she thinks of it in those
terms as did Oberyn. I don’t think Oberyn

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:54.519
thought of himself as Bi-Sexual I think he
just really liked having sex with anything

00:03:54.519 --> 00:03:56.010
that caught his eye.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:04:00.409
If you’re a torchwood fan, think of them
like Captain Jack, anything that moves.

00:04:00.409 --> 00:04:05.120
She’s a little more hot-headed than Obara
and like a high born person, isn’t as inclined

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:08.860
to obey. On the show you can probably expect
her reaction to Oberyn’s death to be the

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:10.500
craziest of all the Sand Snakes.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:14.180
Again, there are some interesting things the
show will probably do with her that I’ll

00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.650
mention during the spoiler section.

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:20.919
moving on to Tyene. On the show she’s being
played by Rosabell Laurenti Sellers. In the

00:04:20.919 --> 00:04:24.830
books she reminds me a lot of Arya if the
Starks hadn’t all been split up. Tyene is

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:28.139
the daughter of a Septa, it’s implied that
she’s from Highgarden. We never find out

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:32.080
what her name is either but there are some
theories I’ll explain in a sec.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:35.520
It’s not stated specifically her mother
is from Highgarden, but because in the books

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:39.660
it says Princess Arianne and a few of the
Sand Snakes visited Tyene’s mother after

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:45.650
crossing the Mander, that’s the river that
flows through the Reach where Highgarden is.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:49.830
There was also an incident later when Tyene
and Arianne plotted to marry Arianne to Willas

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:53.820
Tyrell, that’s Loras’ older brother. He’s
the heir to Highgarden but he’s a cripple

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:54.570
with a bad leg.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:04:57.169
It’s probably something the show isn’t
going to deal with, mostly because it’s

00:04:57.169 --> 00:05:00.570
an Arianne backstory thing. But Prince Doran,
Arianne’s father Prince Doran who’s being

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.039
played by Alexander Siddig is also a cripple.

00:05:03.039 --> 00:05:06.330
Tyene’s weapon of choice is poison. Oberyn
is described as having a love of poison’s,

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:12.180
the show paid homage to it when that kid was
coating his spear in poison before Tyrion’s

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:12.479
trial.

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.560
There’s a really cool theory about the true
identity of Tyene’s mother. Septa Lemore

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:19.160
is the best theory I’ve seen and it would
make Tyene the heir to the Eyrie. That’s

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.490
the place where Sansa and Littlefinger were.
Robin Arryn is currently the heir even though

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.400
he might really be Littlefinger’s child.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.289
Parentage and bloodlines in Game of Thrones
is very complicated. Everyone is a complete

00:05:26.289 --> 00:05:30.419
whore in the best possible way. There are
countless people on the show that are closely

00:05:30.419 --> 00:05:34.699
related to other big characters from other
great houses without knowing it, just because

00:05:34.699 --> 00:05:39.500
everyone’s parents were every bit the whores
that Cersei, Jaime and all the younger people

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:46.220
are.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.560
The reason Tyene might be an heir to the Eyrie
is because instead of Septa Lemore it’s

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:53.530
possible that Tyene’s mother was one of
the daughters of Alys Arryn and Elys Waynwood.

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:58.009
The show didn’t got into their characters,
but Alys is the sister of Jon Arryn, father

00:05:58.009 --> 00:06:00.210
of Robin Arryn, who we have met.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:03.949
The Waynwoods had two daughters that became
septas. One of those daughters was seduced

00:06:03.949 --> 00:06:09.550
by a sellsword and had a child. This is all
from Feast for Crows chapter 41 or Alayne

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:16.550
2 depending on which copy of the book you’re
reading.

00:06:17.259 --> 00:06:24.259
It’s possible that that sellsword was really
Oberyn Martell. Tyene would have been born

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:31.009
around the time Ellia was betrothed to Rhaegar
Targaryen, so it’s possible that to avoid

00:06:31.009 --> 00:06:35.970
a scandal with Dorne and The Crown, the Waynwoods
covered up the true identity of the sellsword

00:06:35.970 --> 00:06:37.539
and said that the child died.

00:06:37.539 --> 00:06:41.400
It’s not ironclad evidence or anything,
but Tyene is one of 8 daughters and Alys Arryn,

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:45.120
her supposed grandmother was one of eight
daughters.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.419
It could just be a coincidence or George RR
Martin could have intended for us to draw

00:06:48.419 --> 00:06:49.870
that conclusion.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.120
Also if you have read the books and you know
who Harry Harding is, he’s a proven Arryn

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.250
and he and Tyene have the same signature dimples
on their face

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:01.680
It’s not a theory that’s going to bear
any fruit on the show. But it’s just a really

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:05.259
interesting subplot in the books. In real
life history, things like this happened all

00:07:05.259 --> 00:07:09.410
the time. People from noble families had bastards
with other prominent families and they covered

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:10.870
it up to avoid scandal.

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:15.580
Here’s a crazy theory, what if Oberyn Martell
was secretly whoring himself out all over

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:21.220
the world as part of some super long plot.
Like he created heirs connected to specific

00:07:21.220 --> 00:07:24.960
major powers in the east and the major houses
in westeros. Usually alliances like that are

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.169
made with children.

00:07:28.169 --> 00:07:31.650
I don’t think that’s what was really going
on, I think he was just a man whore. But it’s

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:37.750
fun to think that he intentionally created
a Dornish heir to the Eyrie.

00:07:37.750 --> 00:07:41.120
Tyene is the last Sand Snake the show is doing,
the younger five are all still minor characters

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:41.910
but they’re all very interesting.

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:46.240
Sarella is the next oldest, she’s the daughter
of a Trader from the summer aisles. We don’t

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:51.680
hear her name, but we know the mother captains
a ship called the Feathered Kiss. Remember,

00:07:51.680 --> 00:07:55.590
that’s where Grey Worm is supposed to be
from. So Sarella would have the same dark

00:07:55.590 --> 00:07:56.460
skin as him.

00:07:56.460 --> 00:08:02.099
There’s a pretty strong theory that Sarella
is masquerading as a character named Alleras

00:08:02.099 --> 00:08:07.199
in Oldtown during Book 4. Mostly because Alleras
is Sarella spelled backwards. But because

00:08:07.199 --> 00:08:10.330
a lot of you probably haven’t read book
4 yet I won’t talk about her character too

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:15.259
much because Alleras crosses paths with people
on the show.

00:08:15.259 --> 00:08:19.050
The reason she’s probably not on the show
is because her part is very minor and she

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:24.139
won’t be doing a lot until Winds of Winter.
But because she gets tied up with people on

00:08:24.139 --> 00:08:27.229
the show. They might cast her in season 6
or 7.

00:08:27.229 --> 00:08:34.229
Next are the four daughters of Ellaria Sand,
the woman we met on the show. Ellaria is a

00:08:34.589 --> 00:08:39.349
bastard but she’s like Jon Snow, she’s
the daughter of nobles. Her father is Lord

00:08:39.349 --> 00:08:42.830
Harmen Uller. House Uller are bannermen of
the Martells in Dorne. So she and her children

00:08:42.830 --> 00:08:46.080
all descend from royalty, but they’re still
named as bastards.

00:08:46.080 --> 00:08:48.680
The reason the show probably isn’t doing
them is because they also have very small

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:50.640
parts in book 4 and 5.

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:54.130
Elia is the oldest, she’s about 14 which
makes her pretty close to Arya’s age. She

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:59.850
is supposed to have a big storyline with Arianne
Martell in Winds of Winter.

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:05.279
Next is Obella, she’s about 12. Then There’s
Dorea, she’s about 8 and Loreza is the youngest

00:09:05.279 --> 00:09:07.870
Sand Snake. She’s about 7.

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:11.830
Interesting side note, in the books Lord Harmen
Ellaria’s father traveled to King’s Landing

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:15.700
for Joffrey and Margeary’s wedding. But
the show didn’t cast him, they cut him out.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:19.649
But in the books he was there for the Purple
Wedding.

00:09:19.649 --> 00:09:26.649
Season 5 is mostly going to draw from Book
4 and book 5. Mostly book 4 though. The show

00:09:28.899 --> 00:09:33.610
will probably change the Obara, Nymeria and
Tyene to give them bigger parts than they

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:37.450
had in the books. If anything they’ll just
take Arianne’s story and give it to them.

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:42.740
Here’s where I need to get into specifics,
so careful for spoilers from book 4 in case

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:49.100
you haven’t read it. You can just skip forward
in the video like 45 seconds. I’ll wait

00:09:49.100 --> 00:09:51.500
just a sec...okay, here we go.

00:09:51.500 --> 00:09:55.830
In the book Arianne wants to rally support
for Mrycella to take the Iron Throne, of all

00:09:55.830 --> 00:10:01.930
the characters directly involved in that plot
only Mrycella, Hotah, Obara, Tyene, Nymeria

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:04.730
and Prince Doran have been cast.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:11.730
Also, there was a casting sheet that leaked.
It showed Jaime being in Dorne with Bronn.

00:10:15.610 --> 00:10:19.500
Which is a vast departure from the books.
Here’s what I think they’re doing.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.260
They’ll still do the Myrcella plot but give
her a more active role. They recast her part

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:26.230
and scheduling conflicts had nothing to do
with it. It think they felt like Aimee Richardson,

00:10:26.230 --> 00:10:29.730
the actress playing her in season 4 wasn’t
right for the story they were giving Myrcella.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:33.760
So they cast someone older. Nell Tiger Free
is the new actress. They did the same thing

00:10:33.760 --> 00:10:36.890
with Tommen, so this isn’t a new thing.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:41.130
The big fight where the Darkstar comes for
Myrcella will probably be a battle between

00:10:41.130 --> 00:10:45.480
Jaime, Bronn and Obara. I don’t think they’ll
chop off Myrcella’s ear. They didn’t chop

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:49.570
off Tyrion’s nose after Blackwater. But
the big oh shit fight will still probably

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:53.959
happen. They’ll just subtract Arys Oakheart
and the Darkstar and add in Jaime and Bronn.

00:10:53.959 --> 00:10:58.860
This raises a lot of questions for Jaime’s
whereabouts in book 4 because he goes somewhere

00:10:58.860 --> 00:11:02.620
totally different in the books, but it makes
sense that the show would narrow it’s focus

00:11:02.620 --> 00:11:03.450
to Dorne.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:07.980
I still think Nymeria and Tyene will head
to King’s Landing by the end of the season

00:11:07.980 --> 00:11:11.930
and we’ll see the crossover with the High
Sparrow. Being played by Jonathan Pryce.

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:18.930
There was also reports of a huge scene with
a shitload of extras being filmed at a big

00:11:22.360 --> 00:11:29.360
bull ring in spain, complete with bulls. I’m
going to save that for a future video, but

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:45.600
if you’ve read the books. You know what
scene that is. So get excited.

